{"id": "EUVD-2026-101064", "enisaUuid": "3b702908-c674-3406-b199-100b7026bf20", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsoc: samsung: exynos-pmu: fix use-after-free of interrupt generator node\n\nThe setup_cpuhp_and_cpuidle() parses the device tree node for the\ninterrupt generation block via of_parse_phandle() and decrements its\nreference count using of_node_put() immediately after fetching the resource\naddress. However, later the intr_gen_node pointer is passed into\nof_syscon_register_regmap().\n\nFix this by declaring intr_gen_node with __free() and removing\nof_node_put().", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4450102d6aa2a85b1d2d8610920fcbe45eb0ef69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/164313e24cb0f51528bc2099c5564174ead11d8a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dd1999783d7d12434006289338373e49492dc96"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x8m9-w5rv-ggmr", "CVE-2026-98415"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "250b7057-ab36-3999-96d6-443cb5182afd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78b72897a5c8bb9d3b51fc6494a1eb09265487a4 <4dd1999783d7d12434006289338373e49492dc96"}, {"id": "47eec228-fa85-343d-b8cd-1d0fad7df710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4c254d62-bb7d-3499-8c7e-722aa0644159", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "7a97846e-57a3-3803-a9fc-f37163ab75c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78b72897a5c8bb9d3b51fc6494a1eb09265487a4 <4450102d6aa2a85b1d2d8610920fcbe45eb0ef69"}, {"id": "82634f32-cfa8-38d2-8b74-bcc64aa7d2de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ba51e691-ae67-38ec-acb8-bdde4bcfd0f7", "product": {"name": "Li